    "q-76954": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76954",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $7≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n\nII. $36≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\nIII. $26≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true because $6∣(7-(-5)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(7-(-5))÷6=12÷6=2\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true because $3\\,|\\,(36-0).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(36-0)÷3=36÷3=12\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false because $4∤(26-9).$ Notice that $26-9=17,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
