    "q-212524": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212524",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that $-8≡-17\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nI. $n=7$\n\nII. $n=8$\n\nIII. $n=9$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-8-(-17)=9.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $7∤9.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=7.$\n\n- Note that $8∤9.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $9∣9$ because $9÷9=1,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
